{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:0.4", "PA_ja_204:1.1"], "en": "4. The Vīraka Jātaka “Have you seen, Vīraka,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:1.2"], "en": "the sweet-voiced bird?”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:1.3", "PA_ja_204:1.4"], "en": "\"My husband, who resembles a peacock's neck and is adorned with a crest.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:2.1"], "en": "\"Of the bird that moves both on water and on land,\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:2.2"], "en": "“Constantly feeding on raw fish;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:2.3"], "en": "Savitthaka, imitating him,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:2.4"], "en": "died, entangled in the water-moss.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_204:3.1"], "en": "The Vīraka Jātaka, the fourth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
